ilya2@rcn.com wrote:
> [Breaking a wand of digging...]
> 
> 1. What happens to the square YOU are standing on?

If it happens to generate a hole on the square you are standing on, you
can fall through in the same turn.

> 2. If your pet or some peaceful monster falls through a new hole and
> dies, do you lose luck?

Nothing loses health from falling down a hole, I believe (correct me if
wrong). If the dig "blast" kills your pet, the death is a standard
"rumble of distant thunder", and is -15 alignment with -1 luck.

Now, pits. I don't think you are responsible when your pet falls into a
/oDigging pit and dies, because the "responsibility" code checks for
whether you displaced it in. But I could be wrong.

> 3. If you break the wand in a temple, and the priest falls into
> pit/hole, what happens?

Well, for the priest to fall into pit on the turn of wandbreak, s/he has
to be within range of the wandblast - meaning s/he will get angry in any
case.

You are allowed to dig in a temple, so I don't think that exploding a
wand elsewhere

> 4. What if pit or hole appears under the altar?

Hmm. Either this is a bug or a wizmode effect. Not sure which. When not
levitating, the message is "A [pit/hole] appears [on/in] the altar.",
and the altar disappears. When levitating, the altar message becomes a
floor message ("A [pit/hole] appears [on/in] the floor."), and the altar
disappears.

On the other hand, it seems like a pit or hole can coexist if forced to
in wizmode.

